# ── MON-87 migration image (docker/migration/Dockerfile) ────────────────────────
# The stock flyway/flyway base bundles JDBC drivers for databases MONTEIS does not use
# (SQL Server, Cassandra, Couchbase, GCP Spanner, Databricks, Mongo, ...). Those unused
# drivers + their netty / httpcore5 / shaded-jackson transitive jars carry HIGH CVEs
# for code paths the Postgres-only migration Job never loads. We waive them by id here
# CVEs in the Postgres driver, the flyway engine, the JRE, or the OS are
# deliberately NOT listed and still fail the gate.
# Re-audit this list whenever the flyway base image digest is bumped.
#
# com.microsoft.sqlserver:mssql-jdbc (SQL Server driver)
CVE-2025-59250
# io.netty — netty-handler / netty-codec-http(2) / netty-codec-compression
# (Cassandra / Couchbase / GCP Spanner transports)
CVE-2026-44249
CVE-2026-45416
CVE-2026-50010
CVE-2026-55831
CVE-2026-55833
CVE-2026-56745
CVE-2026-56819
CVE-2026-59901
CVE-2026-75595
# org.apache.httpcomponents.core5:httpcore5 / httpcore5-h2 (Cassandra driver)
CVE-2026-54399
CVE-2026-54428
# jackson 2.18.7 SHADED inside databricks-jdbc (flyway's own jackson 2.22.0/3.1.4,
# used by the Postgres migration path, is a different version and is NOT affected)
CVE-2026-54512
CVE-2026-54513
GHSA-r7wm-3cxj-wff9
# jackson SHADED inside databricks-jdbc (2.18.7), couchbase core-io (2.21.4) and
# aws-secretsmanager-jdbc (2.22.2). flyway's own jackson in 13.9.0 (2.22.3 / 3.1.7)
# is fixed, so these ids only hit the unused drivers
CVE-2026-68494
CVE-2026-68497
CVE-2026-89407
CVE-2026-89425
CVE-2026-91776
CVE-2026-91777
# at.yawk.lz4:lz4-java (Cassandra driver, via cassandra-jdbc-wrapper / java-driver-core 4.19.2)
# flyway 13.10.0 still ships the same driver, so bumping the base does not fix it
CVE-2026-106451
